9M market cap on $251M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -2% over the past three years and +8% annually across the full decade \u2014 essentially flat, and a business treading water is rarely a path to compounding.","Returns on capital run at 3% against a 7% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 12.8\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 0.5\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 7.7% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 13% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.4) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Payout ratio of 4743% leaves essentially no coverage if earnings wobble","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Operating margins 11% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 9.9% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Revenue growth lags most Real Estate peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Real Estate peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"tex